WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:11.440
Ho Ho Ho, Bitches!

00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:20.820
'Tis the season and this week we rollin up some mistletoe with "A Christmas Carol" by Charles Dickens.

00:00:20.820 --> 00:00:26.600
Ebeneezer Scrooge got rep for bein the coldest
honkey you ever seen. This jive-ass fool so damn shysty

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:28.540
that he don’t throw out ends for nobody.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:33.120
Whether it be his worker Bob Cratchit, who needs some coal so he don’t freeze his ass off,

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:37.460
or some playas comin by tryin to help the po folk, Scrooge ain’t givin’ up dat cheddar.

00:00:37.460 --> 00:00:41.360
When Scrooge’s nephew Fred drop in and say “Merry Christmas, playa!

00:00:41.360 --> 00:00:45.660
Tis the season to get yo ass to my party and bottle pop all night long”

00:00:45.660 --> 00:00:47.980
But Scrooge like, “Psh. F**k Christmas.”

00:00:47.980 --> 00:00:54.760
Later dat night, Scrooge chillin up in his crib when BOO! The ghost of his old bidness partna Jacob Marley

00:00:54.760 --> 00:01:00.480
swangs in all decked out in chains. But this fool ain’t icin. These chains gnarly as hell.

00:01:00.480 --> 00:01:03.660
Scrooge like, “J-Money, you look like shit, dawg.”

00:01:03.660 --> 00:01:09.160
Marley say, “Yeah blud, well since I was such a cheap bitch all my life, I gotta wander round the earth with these

00:01:09.160 --> 00:01:15.600
scrub-ass chains jockin my style for eternity. So you best change up yo hustle if you don’t wanna end up like me.

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:19.500
And watch out — cuz three other ghosts
gonna drop in and school you good.”

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:25.260
While Scrooge trying to sleep, a creepy lil ghost callin himself "The Ghost of Christmas Past" show up and say,

00:01:25.260 --> 00:01:29.560
“I’m a take you back in time to show you how bad you f**kin up these days.”

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:35.240
Back in the day, Scrooge knew how important it was to roll with a crew and how a real playa treats his workers.

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:38.960
Lookin back at his old self, Scrooge starts feelin mad regret.

00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:45.360
Next the fat-ass Ghost of Christmas Present take him to the Cratchit crib, where Bob’s broke ass tryin to feed his family,

00:01:45.360 --> 00:01:47.840
including his crippled-ass son, Tiny Tim.

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:53.000
Even though life dealt him a shitty hand, Tiny Tim so damn nice it make Scrooge get all soft.

00:01:53.000 --> 00:01:57.700
Then the ghost takes him to Fred’s Christmas party,
which actually look like a pretty chill spot.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:02.040
Scrooge wanna stay but the Ghost like “naw
bruh. There’s somebody else you gotta meet.”

00:02:02.040 --> 00:02:08.160
Last, a hood-ass brutha rolls up on Scrooge and show him a bunch of folk talkin smack about some dead fool.

00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:12.040
Ain’t nobody miss him, and a few people even riding high now that he dead.

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:17.320
When the ghost brings Scrooge to a graveyard, he sees his own damn name on the tombstone!

00:02:17.320 --> 00:02:22.280
Oh sh*t. Then Scrooge like, “Aight, aight, I get it son —&nbsp;I'll change my ways!”

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:25.900
Next morning, Scrooge wake up all geeked that it's Christmas Day.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:29.520
He run into the streets, hollerin at playas, wishin em a Merry Christmas.

00:02:29.520 --> 00:02:34.540
Fool even send a big-ass turkey to the Cratchit family so they can get they grub on like a G.

00:02:34.540 --> 00:02:39.160
From here on out, Scrooge looks after Tiny Tim like another daddy, gives money to the po,

00:02:39.160 --> 00:02:41.800
and loves Christmas for the rest of his
days.

00:02:45.280 --> 00:02:50.020
Now unless you trippin, you know dis play preachin dat Christmas is da most legit time of da year.

00:02:50.020 --> 00:02:53.380
But it ain’t just dat holy talk gettin Charlie D all riled up.

00:02:53.380 --> 00:02:59.260
Christmas all about finding a time of the year where we can put the hustle aside, keep dem swishers lit,

00:02:59.270 --> 00:03:01.830
and show each other love. Like Freddy say,

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:07.140
I have always though of Christmas time...as a good time. a kind, forgiving, charitable, pleasant time. the only time

00:03:07.140 --> 00:03:12.080
I know of, in the long calendar of the year, when men and women seem by one consent to open their

00:03:12.080 --> 00:03:17.560
shut-up hearts freely, and to think of people below them as if they really were fellow-passengers to the grave,

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:20.400
and not another race of creatures bound on other journeys."

00:03:20.400 --> 00:03:27.660
In the 1840s, Chuckie D said he wanted to do two things: Inspire homies to enjoy life and make the lives of the po better.

00:03:27.660 --> 00:03:32.820
That’s one of the reasons that at at the beginning, Dicky showin how much of a hard-ass bitch rich folk can be

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:37.340
when dealin with the po. But when the ghost of Christmas past takes us back to before Scrooge

00:03:37.340 --> 00:03:43.060
start sippin dat Haterade, we see a vulerable, sympathetic cat who the audience start feelin for.

00:03:43.060 --> 00:03:46.500
This ain’t just a Christmas Story, and it ain’t just a ghost story.

00:03:46.500 --> 00:03:52.480
It’s also spittin some mad game bout a twisted-ass society where errybody just lookin out for numba one,

00:03:52.480 --> 00:03:58.360
and only the bottom line matters. At first, Scrooge don’t give a f**k bout the fact that Cratchitt can’t feed his family.

00:03:58.360 --> 00:04:02.700
All he care about is da change he gonna lose
by letting Bobby-boy take a day off.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:07.660
But at the end, Scrooge realize dat yo employee ain’t
just some tool you use to stack cheddar.

00:04:07.660 --> 00:04:13.240
He's yo brutha too. Cuz we a society, yo. And in
a society, we gotta watch each other’s backs.

00:04:13.240 --> 00:04:17.320
Look, we all got the power to help a brutha
out and make the world a better place,

00:04:17.320 --> 00:04:22.819
no matter how small our actions may seem. So this holiday season, reach out and do somethin

00:04:22.819 --> 00:04:25.799
righteous for yo fellow homie — like hittin dat subscribe button!

00:04:25.800 --> 00:04:29.480
Happy Holidays, y’all! Peace.

